      "card_ids": ["C16"],
      "claim": "The closest structural analog, [11C]T-773, showed good brain penetration and striatum-selective accumulation in a monkey PET study, directly supporting meaningful CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "Compound 9a, a moderately similar analog, exhibited significant brain penetration after oral administration in mice with a brain/plasma AUC ratio of 3.49, supporting the potential for meaningful CNS exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "A more distant pyrazole analog showed limited brain exposure in rats with a CSF/unbound plasma ratio of 0.05 and P-gp efflux liability, providing a contradictory but low-similarity data point.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The closest analog demonstrates good brain penetration in a direct PET study, and another orally dosed analog shows high brain/plasma exposure. Negative CNS-penetration evidence comes from much more structurally distant compounds, so the overall experimental record supports meaningful CNS access.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific pharmacokinetic or brain exposure data are available; the prediction relies on analogical transfer.",
    "Most negative records are from analogs with low Morgan similarity (<0.32), limiting their relevance.",
    "The closest positive analog is a PET radiotracer, so quantitative steady-state brain exposure for the unlabeled query is not directly established."
  ],
